# Organizational BNPL

- Repo: organizational BNPL product with UI under `ui/organization-panel` and backend under `service/organization-panel-service`.
- Primary UI: Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript + Material 3 (MUI) in `ui/organization-panel`.
- Primary backend: Spring Boot **4.0.8** (Java) + **PostgreSQL** in `service/organization-panel-service`.
- Backend auth: panel login (`panel_users` + BCrypt) issues JWT; configure `JWT_SECRET`.
- Backend DB tables: **plural** names (see `db-table-naming` rule).
- Backend Java boilerplate: use **Lombok** (see `java-lombok` rule); do not hand-write getters/setters/ctors/loggers.
- Backend entity ↔ DTO mapping: use **MapStruct** (see `java-mapstruct` rule); do not hand-write field copying in services.
- Dev database: `docker-compose-dev` (Postgres **18.6**, db `bnpl_db`).
- Prefer TypeScript strict typing on the UI; avoid `any` unless unavoidable and justified.
- Keep UI and API contracts explicit; do not invent backend endpoints without confirming they exist or documenting assumptions.
- Match existing patterns in this repo when present; do not copy unrelated projects unless asked.
- Prefer small, focused changes; no drive-by refactors.

## Layout

```
ui/organization-panel/                    # Next.js + Material 3 UI
ui/customer-app/                          # Customer Next.js app
ui/admin-panel/                           # Admin Next.js app
service/libs/domain/                      # Shared JPA entities (admin/, panel/)
service/libs/dto/                         # Shared API DTOs (admin/, panel/, customer/, merchant/)
service/organization-panel-service/       # Panel backend (8080)
service/customer-service/                 # Customer backend (8081)
service/admin-service/                    # Admin backend (8082); owns merchants
service/merchant-service/                 # Merchant purchase API (8083)
```
